<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hamengkubuwono I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1717">1717</a>–<a href="/years/1792">1792</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Prince Mangkubumi, Hamengkubuwana I</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hamengkubuwana I, earlier Prince Mangkubumi, was the founder and first sultan of Yogyakarta. A son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amangkurat-iv">Amangkurat IV</a>, he rebelled against his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakubuwono-ii">Pakubuwana II</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-east-india-company">Dutch East India Company</a> in 1746, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-giyanti">Treaty of Giyanti</a> of 1755 divided Mataram between him and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakubuwana-iii">Pakubuwana III</a>. He built the kraton of Yogyakarta and ruled until his death in 1792.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hamengkubuwono-i.jpg" alt="Hamengkubuwono I" width="320" height="393" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Idangmedia · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Raden_Mas_Sujono.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
